# Manda update handoff

When the user asks to update the Manda install or the Manda server, copy only the changed files to both places below. Use the same path the file has under `Mods`. Do not search the disk. Do not print the password.

Use the paths in this rule first. Do not list the FTP root when those remote files are already there.

If the install folder or the remote Mods path is missing, FileZilla is the source. Open only the site named `MandaPanda` in `C:\Users\rft30\AppData\Roaming\FileZilla\sitemanager.xml`. Read host, port, user, and `<Pass>` from that site. Do not look through other sites. Connect with those values and list that login's directory once. The server folder is the one that contains `Mods`. Do not scan the PC for it.

This is separate from the Doom Test handoff. Doom Test updates do not go to Manda unless the user asks.

If the user says **Doom Work**, follow `.cursor/rules/doom-work.mdc`. That copies the files in Downloads into `ZZZ_DoomMod_Standalone` on Manda local, Manda dedicated, Doom Test local, and Doom Test dedicated.

Example files:

- `Mods\ZZZ_DoomMod_Standalone\DoomMultiplayer.dll`
- `Mods\zzzzzAGF-Compatibilities-Doom-v1\SpecialNoEACCompatibilities.dll`

## 1. Manda install

`C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\7 Days to Die - MandaServer\Mods\ZZZ_DoomMod_Standalone\DoomMultiplayer.dll`

`C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\7 Days to Die - MandaServer\Mods\zzzzzAGF-Compatibilities-Doom-v1\SpecialNoEACCompatibilities.dll`

## 2. Manda server

FTP, not SFTP. The connection comes from the FileZilla site `MandaPanda`: host `104.192.227.20`, port `8821`, user `auroragf`. The `<Pass>` text is plain base64. Decode it in the process. Do not put it on a command line.

Remote files:

`104.192.227.20_26920/Mods/ZZZ_DoomMod_Standalone/DoomMultiplayer.dll`

`104.192.227.20_26920/Mods/zzzzzAGF-Compatibilities-Doom-v1/SpecialNoEACCompatibilities.dll`

After each copy, hash the destination and match it to the file you built. A dedicated server keeps the DLL it loaded at startup, so tell the user to restart the Manda server before the change applies.
